<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  com.apple.developer.healthkit / .access were removed here TEMPORARILY.
  The provisioning profile behind IOS_PROVISIONING_PROFILE_BASE64 (GitHub
  secret) doesn't grant HealthKit yet -- requesting it here without a
  matching profile fails the archive step outright (build #91, 2026-08-21:
  "Provisioning profile doesn't include the HealthKit capability").
  Once the App ID has HealthKit enabled on developer.apple.com and the
  profile is regenerated + the secret updated to match, restore:
    <key>com.apple.developer.healthkit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.developer.healthkit.access</key>
    <array/>
  The JS-side Health sync code (native-health.ts, wellness-gate.tsx) is
  untouched and still native-platform-gated -- it'll fail gracefully (a
  toast, not a crash) via its existing try/catch until this is restored.
-->
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>webcredentials:forge-ebhd.onrender.com</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
